{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.TorusKnotDeltaQWrithe","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.TorusKnotDeltaQWrithe","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.GeomSum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TorusKnotDeltaQ.qbracket_eq_div","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TorusKnotDeltaQ.qbracket_eq_div","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/torus-knot-delta-q-writhe.lean#L96-L102","doc":"Over a field with `h = q − q⁻¹ ≠ 0`, the division-free `[w]_q` above is\nliterally the classical quotient `(q^w − q^{-w})/(q − q⁻¹)`.  Nothing is\nlost by carrying the Laurent-polynomial form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TorusKnotDeltaQ.torus_deltaQ_eq_h_qbracket","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TorusKnotDeltaQ.torus_deltaQ_eq_h_qbracket","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/torus-knot-delta-q-writhe.lean#L77-L85","doc":"**`δ_q(T_{m,p}) = h·[(m-1)p]_q`** with `h = q − q⁻¹` — the torus-knot\nq-dimension decoration at the writhe exponent `w = (m-1)p` factors as `h`\ntimes the quantum integer `[(m-1)p]_q`.  Pre-archimedean (no `ℝ`, no `π`);\nsorry-free.  `m = 2` recovers `δ_q(T_{2,k}) = h[k]_q` (`w = k`). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:torus-knot-delta-q-writhe","label":"prop:torus-knot-delta-q-writhe","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/torus-knot-delta-q-writhe.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TorusKnotDeltaQ.deltaQ_eq_h_mul_qbracket","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TorusKnotDeltaQ.deltaQ_eq_h_mul_qbracket","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/torus-knot-delta-q-writhe.lean#L66-L75","doc":"**`δ_q = h·[w]_q` at any exponent `w`**, with `h = q − q⁻¹`.  This is the\ntelescoping identity `(∑_{i<w} xⁱ y^{w−1−i})(x − y) = x^w − y^w`\n(`geom_sum₂_mul`), pure commutative-ring algebra: no hypothesis, no\ndivision. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TorusKnotDeltaQ.torusWrithe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TorusKnotDeltaQ.torusWrithe","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/torus-knot-delta-q-writhe.lean#L62-L64","doc":"Writhe of the standard positive torus braid `(σ₁⋯σ_{m-1})^p`\n(number of positive crossings). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TorusKnotDeltaQ.qbracket","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TorusKnotDeltaQ.qbracket","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/torus-knot-delta-q-writhe.lean#L52-L60","doc":"Quantum integer `[w]_q`, written division-free as the Laurent polynomial\n\n  `[w]_q = ∑_{i<w} qⁱ · q^{-(w-1-i)} = q^{w-1} + q^{w-3} + ⋯ + q^{-(w-1)}`.\n\nIt satisfies `[w]_q · (q − q⁻¹) = q^w − q^{-w}`\n(`deltaQ_eq_h_mul_qbracket`), which was the previous *definition* — a\nquotient, hence meaningful only where `q − q⁻¹ ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TorusKnotDeltaQ.deltaQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TorusKnotDeltaQ.deltaQ","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/torus-knot-delta-q-writhe.lean#L49-L50","doc":"q-dimension decoration `δ_q = q^w − q^{-w}` at writhe `w`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}